      "answer": {
        "text": "⚠️ Do not drive your truck until it is repaired if it is covered by NHTSA's \"park it\" air bag recalls 18V022000, 18V023000, 17V787000 or 17V788000. These cover front air bag inflators on some 2006 Rangers that can explode in a crash and throw metal fragments. Call Ford at 1-866-436-7332 or a Ford dealer. The repair is free, and Ford may be able to arrange a tow or a mobile repair.\n\nNHTSA lists 12 recalls in total for the 2006 Ranger. Most of them cover only certain trucks, and the rest are also mostly about air bags:\n- 16V036000 and 15V322000: earlier air bag inflator fixes, replaced by the final repairs above\n- 23V306000 (replaces 23V125000): checks whether replacement passenger inflators were installed correctly\n- 21V076000 and 21V081000: replacement-part air bag inflators that may explode\n- 11V352000: multi-function switch service part that can stop turn signals and brake lights from working\n- 05V520000: wiper motor gear may be missing grease\n\nI can't see whether a recall is still open on your particular truck. To check, enter your 17-digit VIN at nhtsa.gov/recalls or call Ford. You can also send me the VIN and I'll decode it to confirm the details.",
